cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PalynoPro: quantitative pollen morphometry from electron micrographs"
abstract: >-
  PalynoPro is a self-contained web application for the quantitative morphometry of pollen
  grains in scanning electron micrographs, entirely in the browser, with no installation, no
  third-party libraries and no server-side computation. It reads whole folders of instrument
  TIFF, PNG or JPEG images, takes the group and grain from the file name or from an index,
  computes the pixel size from the magnification and checks it against the printed scale bar,
  which it finds by itself. It segments each grain, reads its outline in 720 directions,
  removes the spines by a grey-scale opening of the radial profile to measure the corpus
  (equivalent diameter, Feret widths, elongation, circularity), counts and measures the spines,
  detects the lumina of the reticulum by a local threshold, and measures surface texture by
  grey-level co-occurrence. On overview images it classifies grains as turgid or collapsed by
  the solidity of the corpus, excluding aggregates, fragments and grains on the edge, with
  Wilson intervals and a chi-square test among groups. Groups are compared with the grain as
  the unit: analysis of variance with Tukey letters, Kruskal-Wallis with Holm adjustment,
  principal components, PERMANOVA, linear discriminant analysis and random forest validated by
  leaving out one grain at a time. A report with the methods, every figure, a gallery of
  measured grains and references is produced for printing. Bilingual interface (Spanish and
  English). The statistical engines were checked against independent implementations in R
  (6,705 comparisons in 18 families, none out of tolerance), the image engine against
  simulated grains of known truth, and 155 unit tests run in the browser.
